A||||1||Lynx||Temp Gauge reads WAY low!
Z||000000||Lynx||06-02-99||11:40 AM||||Ok i just had a problem with a water leak on the thermostat housing gasket. First it blew out then i replaced it and it still leaked a little so i fixed it agian with more silicon and put in some Bars stop leak to make sure nothing leaked. Then just to make everthing perfect i put in a new 180 thermostat. OK ever since all this stuff happened the temp gauge is reading WAY low like more than 60 degrees. It shows that the engine in hot traffic is onle like 150. And i know its higher because the fan kicked on once. Im going to buy another temp sensor. I just want to know if anything else can cause this but the temp sensor?
Z||000001||theogre||06-02-99||12:25 PM||||if I recall, that is the sensor on the filler neck isn't it? ((I can never remember wich flaming one is which))<p>Asumming it's the one I think it is.... you screwed up the ground for it. that sensor has 2 leads, on for the gauge, one to the over temp light. If the neck isn't grounding to the block right, it will throw the gauge off. (all these sensors, with the posible exception of the ECM one, are resistance or switched to ground)<p>you can check the running temp by scanning the ECM, wich will also tell you the block temp. the ECM uses yet another temp sensor some place else on the motor.
